# Phase 12: Persistence & Sync — P1 (Session Continuity + Edge-Cloud)
# Status: NOT STARTED
# Depends on: Phase 11 (runtime integration)
# Blocks: None (independent of 13/14)

## Goal
Persist PipelineStats and spilled content across sessions and sync
between edge (CLI) and cloud (server) for seamless session continuity.

## Why
- PipelineStats (cache ratios, token estimates) take 3-5 turns to warm up
- Without persistence, every session restart loses learned behavior
- Spilled content (tool results moved to disk) must survive process restart
- Edge-cloud sync enables session handoff (start on mobile, continue on desktop)

## Tasks

### 12.1 — PipelineStats Persistence
- [ ] Define serialization format for PipelineStats (JSON or bincode)
- [ ] Save PipelineStats to session record on session pause/end
- [ ] Load PipelineStats from session record on session resume
- [ ] Schema: add `pipeline_stats BLOB` column to sessions table
- [ ] Migration: backward-compatible (NULL = fresh stats, no breakage)
- [ ] Unit test: serialize/deserialize round-trip preserves all fields

### 12.2 — Spill Storage Backend
- [ ] Define SpillBackend trait: store(key, content) → SpillRef, load(ref) → content
- [ ] Implement LocalFsSpillBackend (current: /tmp or configurable dir)
- [ ] Implement CloudSpillBackend (S3/object storage for server-side)
- [ ] SpillRef carries backend hint (local vs cloud) for transparent load
- [ ] TTL-based cleanup: spills older than session TTL are garbage collected
- [ ] Unit test: store/load round-trip, TTL expiry, missing key handling

### 12.3 — Session Continuity Protocol
- [ ] On session save: serialize PipelineStats + active spill refs
- [ ] On session load: deserialize stats, verify spill refs still accessible
- [ ] Handle stale spills gracefully (content gone → re-fetch or mark unavailable)
- [ ] SessionLatches persistence: latched values survive session resume
- [ ] EmergentContext carry-forward: persist discovered skills/memory across restarts

### 12.4 — Edge-Cloud Sync (extends existing cloud sync)
- [ ] Include PipelineStats in session sync payload
- [ ] Include spill content in sync (small spills inline, large spills by ref)
- [ ] Conflict resolution: latest-write-wins for stats, merge for spill catalog
- [ ] Sync protocol: existing outbox pattern (no new transport needed)
- [ ] Test: start session on edge, sync to cloud, resume on cloud with warm stats

### 12.5 — Warm Start Optimization
- [ ] On new session with same agent+model: seed stats from historical average
- [ ] Cross-session percentile pooling: response token estimates shared per model
- [ ] First-turn heuristic: if no stats, use model defaults (skip cold 3 turns)
- [ ] Test: warm-started session achieves target cache ratio 2 turns faster

## Acceptance Criteria
- PipelineStats round-trip through persistence without data loss
- Session resume within 50ms overhead (stats deserialization budget)
- Spilled content survives process restart on same machine
- Edge→Cloud sync delivers warm stats within 1 sync cycle
- No regression in session startup time (< 100ms total)

## Key Files
- astra-turn-core/src/context_feedback.rs (PipelineStats struct)
- services/src/sessions/ (session persistence layer)
- services/src/cloud_sync/ (edge-cloud sync protocol)
- runtime/src/server/session_lifecycle.rs (save/load hooks)
